From: Fedora/Cygwin
Subject: Disable loadable builtins installation

This patch removes the installation of loadable builtins from the
make install target. The Fedora rationale (April 2002) was FHS compliance:
the loadable examples are considered sample code that shouldn't be
installed in system directories like /usr/lib/bash.

INTENTIONALLY NOT APPLIED in this repository because:
- We want to investigate/enable loadable modules support on Cygwin
- Debian provides these as a separate 'bash-builtins' package
- The examples are useful for testing dynamic loading functionality

To disable loadable builtins installation, apply this patch:
  patch -p1 < cygwin-patches/DISABLE/no-loadable-builtins.patch

--- a/Makefile.in
+++ b/Makefile.in
@@ -XXX,7 +XXX,6 @@ install:	.made installdirs
 		infodir=$(infodir) htmldir=$(htmldir) DESTDIR=$(DESTDIR) $@ )
 	-( cd $(DEFDIR) ; $(MAKE) $(MFLAGS) DESTDIR=$(DESTDIR) $@ )
 	-( cd $(PO_DIR) ; $(MAKE) $(MFLAGS) DESTDIR=$(DESTDIR) $@ )
-	-( cd $(LOADABLES_DIR) && $(MAKE) $(MFLAGS) DESTDIR=$(DESTDIR) $@ )
 
 install-strip:
 	$(MAKE) $(MFLAGS) INSTALL_PROGRAM='$(INSTALL_PROGRAM) -s' \
